WEBVTT

00:00.490 --> 00:02.470
If I told you to die...

00:02.470 --> 00:04.330
Would you die?

01:15.070 --> 01:39.200
First frame of video starts here.

01:39.070 --> 01:46.240
In an empty world, I recall the day which I cannot recover from.

01:46.780 --> 01:53.960
Smoke blows before my frozen fingertips.

01:54.420 --> 02:01.720
As I pursue memories that cannot be erased despite being soaked with rain,

02:02.170 --> 02:09.640
The shadow of time that is entangled in darkness acts as my key of pain.

02:10.930 --> 02:12.690
Find out

02:12.690 --> 02:15.770
Find out lost days

02:15.770 --> 02:18.110
For my life

02:31.450 --> 02:33.370
Key of Pain

02:35.510 --> 02:39.180
I'll find it out

02:39.300 --> 02:44.970
For your life

03:15.880 --> 03:17.830
How much longer is he going to make me wait?

03:23.010 --> 03:23.760
Kayama!

03:24.550 --> 03:25.590
I'm sorry, sir!

03:25.590 --> 03:27.130
I'll try reaching him one more time.

03:28.770 --> 03:32.180
I don't know what would possess a man to be so late on this important deal.

03:32.180 --> 03:33.380
Kuzuya-san.

03:33.380 --> 03:37.550
Don't you think it's about time you told the rest of us...

03:37.550 --> 03:40.020
...about your precious business partner?

03:42.710 --> 03:43.220
Reiji!

03:43.220 --> 03:46.020
You're just a newbie here, so mind your own business!

03:48.510 --> 03:50.500
This business partner that you found... "Kotetsu," was it?

03:50.500 --> 03:54.400
Are you sure we can trust its ringleader?

03:55.120 --> 03:55.940
What?

03:55.940 --> 03:58.730
I've never heard of a Chinese buyer with that name.

03:59.270 --> 04:00.580
You miserable little...

04:00.580 --> 04:04.690
For someone who's been our inside informer for only half a month, you've sure got a high-and-mighty attitude! Know your place!

04:05.520 --> 04:07.700
The length of time that someone has been around in this organization doesn't matter.

04:07.700 --> 04:10.930
What's most important is how much we can <i>trust</i>  that person.

04:10.930 --> 04:12.120
Am I wrong?

04:14.410 --> 04:15.750
Shouhei Kuzuya!

04:20.140 --> 04:20.800
Die!

04:28.290 --> 04:29.070
Reiji!

04:36.110 --> 04:36.730
Damn it!

04:36.730 --> 04:37.650
Don't let him escape!

04:37.650 --> 04:38.320
Kayama-san!

04:43.280 --> 04:44.660
Bastard...

04:45.650 --> 04:46.830
Who the fuck are you?

04:51.900 --> 04:52.700
Answer me!

04:52.700 --> 04:53.230
Who–?!

04:56.210 --> 04:57.210
Watch where you're fucking driving!

04:58.430 --> 05:00.020
W-What the hell?

05:05.470 --> 05:06.020
Huh?

05:06.020 --> 05:07.080
Damn...

05:07.080 --> 05:08.470
Where did Kayama-san go?

05:12.570 --> 05:14.100
Reiji, are you all right?

05:14.100 --> 05:15.610
It's not deep.

05:16.420 --> 05:18.560
I can't believe he actually did it.

05:18.560 --> 05:19.610
What do you mean?

05:20.400 --> 05:22.960
Your right-hand man, Kayama.

05:23.720 --> 05:28.990
He told me to help him murder you tonight, in the very seat you were sitting in, so he could become Asaya's leader.

05:29.460 --> 05:30.640
What?

05:30.640 --> 05:31.280
Just goes to show...

05:32.020 --> 05:33.510
You trust your pals too much.

05:35.950 --> 05:37.180
Where are you going?

05:37.180 --> 05:40.460
Having a newbie informer around is only going to mess with your important deal, right?

05:41.650 --> 05:42.290
Reiji.

05:48.260 --> 05:48.840
Hello?

05:48.840 --> 05:50.180
That was crap!

05:50.440 --> 05:53.140
I told you to aim for my side, not front and center!

05:53.640 --> 05:55.350
Now my shirt is ruined.

05:55.970 --> 05:56.840
Sorry...

05:56.840 --> 05:58.610
I'll be continuing with my undercover investigation.

05:58.610 --> 05:59.550
Okay.

06:00.020 --> 06:01.450
Be care... ful...

06:02.860 --> 06:05.190
W-Who the hell are you people?

06:05.620 --> 06:09.000
The Greater Kanto area's Narcotics Control Department.

06:09.000 --> 06:10.210
We're Matori.

06:09.000 --> 06:11.660
Note: "Matori" (マトリ) is the Japanese abbreviation for "Narcotics Enforcement Officers."

06:11.660 --> 06:14.700
Narcotics Control Department - Kanto-Shin'etsu Regional Bureau of Health and Welfare

06:17.120 --> 06:20.960
First Criminal
Investigation Division

06:17.340 --> 06:20.960
Not even a high-ranking member like Kayama could give us any revealing information.

06:21.310 --> 06:22.930
The guy's pretty tight-lipped.

06:22.930 --> 06:27.220
There isn't much difference between what we got out of his testimony so far and what we already know.

06:27.220 --> 06:27.880
Director Hiki.

06:28.950 --> 06:34.400
We're positive now that Asaya is the one supplying F.A., the new drug that has surfaced on the streets.

06:35.160 --> 06:36.850
Funny Angel.

06:36.850 --> 06:38.060
Called F.A. for short.

06:38.650 --> 06:41.270
An illegal drug made from unknown materials that is sold by Asaya...

06:41.270 --> 06:44.500
And the one in charge of operating Asaya's business...

06:44.500 --> 06:46.780
...is its broker, Shouhei Kuzuya.

06:47.200 --> 06:53.740
Asaya used to be a middle-level drug organization, but once they began selling F.A., they've shown an alarming growth.

06:53.740 --> 07:00.150
After we obtained information that they intended to expand even further by making some large business deals soon,

07:00.150 --> 07:02.380
we assigned Hal-kun to investigate them undercover.

07:02.690 --> 07:05.180
And there hasn't been much development on this case to date.

07:05.180 --> 07:06.420
That's not so.

07:06.420 --> 07:11.370
We used to believe that the idea of them forming a business partnership with another drug-trafficking group was just a rumor.

07:11.370 --> 07:14.680
Last night's investigation has assured us that this information was, in fact, true.

07:14.680 --> 07:17.560
The Chinese drug-trafficking group Kotetsu...

07:18.400 --> 07:20.520
Have we found any information on Kotetsu?

07:20.520 --> 07:22.980
Nothing's come up, strangely enough.

07:22.980 --> 07:27.400
At the present time, what we know about the size of their organization and the number of members are all based on rumors.

07:27.830 --> 07:30.450
The whole thing about them is weird.

07:30.450 --> 07:32.070
Um... Director Hiki.

07:32.660 --> 07:33.560
What is it?

07:33.560 --> 07:34.680
About Hal...

07:34.680 --> 07:37.450
How long will he be working undercover?

07:40.080 --> 07:42.110
These sales results aren't bad.

07:42.110 --> 07:42.830
But of course.

07:42.830 --> 07:46.890
I'm providing you with info on places where you can sell without being caught by either the Matori or the feds.

07:48.360 --> 07:49.970
How's that wound?

07:49.970 --> 07:51.560
Nothing serious.

07:51.560 --> 07:53.720
Let me off at the next stoplight.

07:53.720 --> 07:55.320
I'll contact you later.

07:55.320 --> 07:58.050
No, I'd like to take you to my hideout from here.

07:58.910 --> 08:02.140
Bringing an outsider informant like me into your confidence, are you?

08:02.140 --> 08:04.400
Aren't you being a little too careless?

08:04.400 --> 08:06.480
You want to know about Kotetsu, don't you?

08:39.380 --> 08:40.720
What's that?

08:40.720 --> 08:42.230
The spare card key to this room.

08:43.360 --> 08:45.230
I'd like you to have it.

08:45.230 --> 08:46.860
I have no reason to take it.

08:46.860 --> 08:48.990
You have no reason not to, either.

08:48.990 --> 08:49.650
Make yourself comfortable.

08:52.600 --> 08:53.890
Can I ask you something?

08:53.890 --> 08:54.320
What is it?

08:55.140 --> 08:59.660
No matter how well I pay you, risking your own life for mine doesn't seem worth the price.

08:59.660 --> 09:01.680
I didn't do it just for the dough.

09:01.680 --> 09:02.790
Then why?

09:02.790 --> 09:05.290
I have a high opinion of you.

09:05.290 --> 09:09.770
There aren't that many brokers around who can expand their enterprise in such a short period like you have.

09:09.770 --> 09:11.130
Keeping you around will keep me from getting bored.

09:11.660 --> 09:14.450
I also had a high opinion of you as an informant.

09:14.450 --> 09:16.970
I've made a surprisingly large amount of money thanks to you.

09:17.350 --> 09:18.780
"Had"?

09:18.780 --> 09:19.980
Past tense?

09:19.980 --> 09:22.140
Yes, things are different now.

09:22.680 --> 09:24.110
Not only do I want your information...

09:24.110 --> 09:26.760
I also want <i>you</i>  on my team.

09:26.760 --> 09:29.610
Asaya's power will grow even larger after we've formed the deal with Kotetsu.

09:30.030 --> 09:32.070
Won't you like to see that up close?

09:41.190 --> 09:43.410
Can I take that as your agreement to our bargain then?

09:45.260 --> 09:46.040
Yeah.

09:53.490 --> 09:56.070
It looks like Hal-kun has successfully managed to infiltrate the Asaya hideout.

09:58.520 --> 09:59.390
So he's all right.

10:00.230 --> 10:01.430
This is...

10:01.430 --> 10:03.860
Kuzuya's cell phone record.

10:03.860 --> 10:05.680
Send it to the Intelligence Division right away!

10:05.680 --> 10:05.930
Kai!

10:06.550 --> 10:07.690
Yes, sir!

10:09.040 --> 10:11.460
So, what's the info on their deal with Kotetsu?

10:12.400 --> 10:17.410
Hal-kun has been allowed to attend their meeting when it takes place, but it seems he still isn't privy to the details.

10:17.410 --> 10:17.900
However...

10:18.470 --> 10:18.950
What's wrong?

10:19.360 --> 10:23.860
With this development, I suspect that the other gang members will be keeping a closer eye on Hal-kun.

10:31.750 --> 10:33.670
Intelligence Division

10:43.170 --> 10:43.960
Etou.

10:45.820 --> 10:46.540
Yes?

10:46.960 --> 10:48.620
Go home and get some sleep.

10:48.620 --> 10:51.580
I'm grateful that you want to help, but it's late.

10:51.580 --> 10:53.460
I'm sorry, Ibu-san.

10:53.460 --> 10:54.770
But I'll be all right.

10:56.420 --> 10:58.250
Hal is in greater danger than I am...

10:58.250 --> 10:59.570
...so I should do something for him...

11:01.300 --> 11:03.220
For Kurabayashi's sake, eh?

11:06.510 --> 11:08.780
Well, if you want a job that's more your field, I've got one right here.

11:15.850 --> 11:17.450
That's right...

11:17.450 --> 11:18.590
Yeah...

11:18.590 --> 11:20.480
...at the usual place...

11:20.480 --> 11:21.480
Yeah.

11:21.480 --> 11:22.720
...time... 25...

11:23.230 --> 11:25.140
I know. That's what I had in mind.

11:25.820 --> 11:26.690
Yeah.

11:26.690 --> 11:28.360
Be discreet as well.

11:28.970 --> 11:30.080
I'm counting on you...

11:30.940 --> 11:32.060
Kitagishi.

11:33.670 --> 11:34.980
Kitagishi?

11:37.770 --> 11:40.600
We've finished analyzing Kuzuya's cell phone records.

11:40.600 --> 11:41.400
Thank you.

11:41.950 --> 11:44.490
Just what I expected of the Intelligence Division. You get your work done fast.

11:44.490 --> 11:46.020
It was all thanks to Etou.

11:46.990 --> 11:48.600
N-Not at all!

11:49.880 --> 11:51.580
Some of these phone numbers are the same.

11:51.580 --> 11:52.550
Yes.

11:52.550 --> 11:57.520
The results show that Kuzuya has been secretly keeping in touch with two people.

11:58.920 --> 11:59.740
Two...

11:59.740 --> 12:02.150
I still have yet to determine the identity of one of them...

12:02.150 --> 12:06.720
But the other one is a man named Kitagishi, who works at a botanical garden on the coast that specializes in tropical flora.

12:07.030 --> 12:09.370
A man who works in a tropical botanic garden... Kitagishi...

12:09.370 --> 12:13.190
A drug broker and a botanical garden employee...

12:13.570 --> 12:15.630
It seems we'll need to investigate.

12:18.910 --> 12:19.400
Director Hiki!

12:21.210 --> 12:22.030
What is it?

12:22.760 --> 12:24.740
Please let me do it!

12:24.740 --> 12:28.740
Eyecatch:-

12:43.350 --> 12:45.110
What huge premises...

12:46.020 --> 12:49.160
I'm Kousaka, here to be interviewed for the part-time position.

12:49.160 --> 12:52.180
How knowledgeable are you on plants?

12:53.450 --> 12:54.770
Um, well...

12:55.570 --> 12:56.520
I like flowers!

12:57.110 --> 13:00.230
The vegetation in these gardens requires a very delicate touch.

13:00.230 --> 13:03.680
If you came here thinking you can play florist and end up screwing something up...

13:03.680 --> 13:05.220
U-Um...

13:04.440 --> 13:05.860
Good morning!

13:06.080 --> 13:07.040
Kagura.

13:07.040 --> 13:08.880
Oh, you're in the middle of a job interview...

13:08.880 --> 13:09.800
I'm sorry to interrupt.

13:11.920 --> 13:12.540
Hello.

13:15.290 --> 13:16.070
Hello!

13:17.400 --> 13:18.840
Actually, you came at the perfect time.

13:19.560 --> 13:21.360
You have very neat handwriting.

13:21.360 --> 13:23.090
The small jobs seem perfect for you,

13:23.530 --> 13:24.950
but how good are you with heavy lifting?

13:24.950 --> 13:27.420
I'm not very confident about that.

13:27.420 --> 13:29.010
But I won't lose to anyone when it comes to willpower!

13:29.010 --> 13:30.090
I see.

13:30.090 --> 13:31.200
At least you're honest.

13:32.540 --> 13:33.640
Kagura...

13:33.640 --> 13:36.170
I think he'll be fine for the position.

13:36.170 --> 13:37.000
And he seems like a diligent worker.

13:37.000 --> 13:39.760
We'll be getting busier as the end of the year approaches,

13:39.760 --> 13:41.980
so the more working hands we have around, the better.

13:42.620 --> 13:44.190
Well, if that's what <i>you</i>  say...

13:44.190 --> 13:46.040
Um...

13:46.040 --> 13:47.220
Thank you for hiring me!

13:47.840 --> 13:50.850
I'm Akito Kagura, a part-time worker here.

13:50.850 --> 13:53.080
Please ask me if there's anything you're unsure of.

13:55.430 --> 13:56.390
I'm Ren Kousaka!

13:56.390 --> 13:59.060
And I have yet to introduce myself.

13:59.700 --> 14:02.800
I'm Kitagishi, head of the research team.

14:03.620 --> 14:05.260
Kitagishi... san?

14:05.470 --> 14:06.410
That's right.

14:06.410 --> 14:09.530
I'm also in charge of designing how the plants here are displayed.

14:09.530 --> 14:10.950
Anyway, be sure to work hard.

14:11.610 --> 14:12.420
Yes, sir.

14:12.420 --> 14:13.620
I'll give it my all.

14:14.610 --> 14:17.420
I've finished checking over all twelve pots of geraniums.

14:17.420 --> 14:20.060
I'll turn on the sprinkler systems for the grass in the southeast area.

14:22.590 --> 14:23.820
This is much heavier than it looks.

14:23.500 --> 14:24.180
Hey!

14:24.180 --> 14:25.310
Get a move on!

14:25.310 --> 14:26.150
Yes, sir!

14:26.830 --> 14:28.340
We've still got 30 more cases to go!

14:28.340 --> 14:28.860
Hurry up!

14:32.080 --> 14:33.070
Come on!

14:33.070 --> 14:33.930
Next!

14:44.280 --> 14:45.490
Almost there...

14:45.490 --> 14:46.640
Okay!

14:52.170 --> 14:53.220
Are you all right?

14:57.650 --> 14:59.050
I–

14:59.050 --> 15:00.190
I'm very sorry!

15:00.190 --> 15:01.420
Thank you!

15:01.420 --> 15:02.660
You're not hurt, are you?

15:02.660 --> 15:03.780
No!

15:03.780 --> 15:06.140
Carrying two of these bags at once is pretty strenuous.

15:07.000 --> 15:07.990
It certainly is...

15:07.990 --> 15:10.240
Why don't I take one from you and we go together?

15:10.690 --> 15:11.110
Okay!

15:18.330 --> 15:19.180
Um, Kagura-san?

15:20.550 --> 15:22.300
What is that building used for?

15:22.300 --> 15:22.920
Oh...

15:23.430 --> 15:25.750
That's the research and development lab.

15:25.750 --> 15:28.040
Research and development lab?

15:28.040 --> 15:30.040
Not only do we work on cultivation research there,

15:30.040 --> 15:34.350
but it's also where we keep plants that need to be nurtured and raised under special conditions.

15:34.350 --> 15:37.680
That's why access to the building is restricted from the regular staff and part-time workers like us.

15:53.620 --> 15:55.600
No problems here.

15:59.600 --> 16:00.740
You idiots!

16:00.740 --> 16:02.810
Handle them with more care!

16:03.420 --> 16:04.150
Watch out!

16:07.210 --> 16:08.660
I-It's all right...

16:08.660 --> 16:10.470
It's only the cover that ripped.

16:10.470 --> 16:12.270
The flower inside is still safe.

16:12.270 --> 16:13.010
Hey!

16:13.010 --> 16:14.680
I told you to carry them gently, didn't I?!

16:14.680 --> 16:15.760
Kitagishi-san!

16:15.760 --> 16:17.540
I'd like to help, if you don't mind!

16:17.540 --> 16:18.890
You little wretch!

16:19.170 --> 16:22.290
This isn't a place for a novice like you to be loitering around in!

16:22.290 --> 16:23.940
Get back to your work!

16:24.940 --> 16:26.610
I-I'm sorry.

16:26.610 --> 16:28.880
Please don't be angry at him, Kitagishi-san.

16:28.880 --> 16:32.780
I haven't explained to him yet how we take in rare species here.

16:32.780 --> 16:33.740
Rare species?

16:34.390 --> 16:36.200
It's my fault.

16:36.200 --> 16:37.160
I'm sorry.

16:38.410 --> 16:41.510
Be sure to tell him then, Kagura.

16:41.510 --> 16:42.600
Honestly...

16:42.600 --> 16:43.850
Kagura-san.

16:43.850 --> 16:46.690
Are those flowers really that important?

16:46.690 --> 16:49.960
Why, yes.
Those black flowers are a member of the orchid family.

16:49.960 --> 16:53.370
Orchidaceae is the largest family of flowering plants in the world,

16:53.370 --> 16:56.710
and those flowers in particular are a new species that has been recently discovered.

16:56.710 --> 16:58.550
They can only be found in one area of the subtropics.

16:59.600 --> 17:01.880
That's why we're still lacking research information on them,

17:01.880 --> 17:06.480
and I think our institute is the only place in Japan where they're allowed to be imported.

17:06.480 --> 17:07.360
I see.

17:08.320 --> 17:11.280
So that's why he's so paranoid about how they're handled.

17:12.140 --> 17:13.940
Black orchids...

17:28.640 --> 17:29.880
You've worked hard today.

17:30.430 --> 17:31.820
Kagura-san!

17:32.990 --> 17:35.220
So you're a university student!

17:35.220 --> 17:37.360
I'm majoring in botany.

17:37.360 --> 17:40.530
What sort of subjects do you learn with a botany major?

17:40.940 --> 17:44.310
Well, what I specifically study is phytogeography,

17:44.310 --> 17:47.480
which is concerned with the research of all plant ecology in general.

17:47.480 --> 17:54.180
For instance, plants are grouped according to what time period and environment they exist in, as well as where they grow natively,

17:54.180 --> 17:56.280
and this is what we call the "flora" of a particular region.

17:56.280 --> 17:58.660
Each plant has differences in their ecosystem.

17:58.660 --> 18:00.320
That's what I find so interesting, and–

18:00.320 --> 18:01.780
Oh, sorry!

18:02.330 --> 18:04.950
I can't stop talking when it comes to plants.

18:04.950 --> 18:05.750
Oh, no...

18:05.750 --> 18:07.630
I was just thinking that you must really like them.

18:08.550 --> 18:09.750
Yeah.

18:10.160 --> 18:14.230
This botanical garden in particular is like my personal heaven on earth.

18:23.550 --> 18:25.900
Their colors and shape are different,

18:25.900 --> 18:27.990
but all of the flowers you see here are orchids.

18:27.990 --> 18:28.730
All of them?

18:28.970 --> 18:33.310
For the rare and wild orchids, we try to display them as they would appear in their natural environment.

18:33.310 --> 18:35.660
This institute holds the greatest number of species within the country.

18:35.660 --> 18:36.840
Wow...

18:36.840 --> 18:39.870
Orchids that are of a different species can still be cross-fertilized,

18:39.870 --> 18:43.860
so even though there are over 1,500 species in the world already, they still continue to keep evolving.

18:45.090 --> 18:48.840
The orchids in this place flourish vibrantly under our care,

18:48.840 --> 18:50.960
and they cheer up everyone who sees them.

18:51.550 --> 18:54.730
It makes me proud to be able to work here.

18:54.730 --> 18:55.980
Kagura-san...

18:57.120 --> 18:59.660
Sorry for monopolizing this conversation.

18:59.660 --> 19:03.760
I was hoping to help you find it a bit more enjoyable working here, but...

19:03.760 --> 19:05.080
You must think I'm a chatterbox.

19:05.080 --> 19:05.810
Oh, no.

19:05.810 --> 19:07.860
I was happy to hear it.

19:07.860 --> 19:09.090
I'll do my best!

19:09.090 --> 19:11.480
Then I'm happy that you're happy.

19:11.990 --> 19:15.200
Let's work hard together so we can finish up tonight's late-night shift.

19:15.200 --> 19:16.460
Okay!

19:16.460 --> 19:17.690
Wait, what?

19:17.690 --> 19:18.810
Late-night shift?

19:18.810 --> 19:20.000
Huh?

19:20.000 --> 19:21.740
Did I forget to mention that?

19:21.740 --> 19:26.660
Grand Exhibition of Orchids
Found Only in
the Western Hemisphere

19:22.250 --> 19:26.320
All of the displays throughout the gardens have to be changed for an event that we're holding during the Christmas season.

19:26.320 --> 19:28.790
But I know that you'll be able to manage, right, Ren-kun?

19:28.790 --> 19:30.970
Y-Yes...

19:30.970 --> 19:32.600
I'll do my best...

19:38.480 --> 19:40.090
And that's Kotetsu.

19:40.090 --> 19:41.130
Yeah.

19:41.930 --> 19:46.240
It's a middle-level Chinese mafia group that has been expanding rapidly with its drugs.

19:46.240 --> 19:51.670
So forming a partnership between your middle-level organizations is what you mean by Asaya's power growing larger?

19:51.670 --> 19:52.680
Yeah.

19:52.680 --> 19:55.990
In exchange for gaining the weapons and drugs that are supplied through Kotetsu's routes,

19:55.990 --> 20:01.210
we will give them the right to own a part of our drug-dealing territory in Japan.

20:01.210 --> 20:02.630
Those are the conditions of our partnership.

20:02.960 --> 20:06.490
So not only will you be able to manufacture your drugs in a more efficient way,

20:06.490 --> 20:09.410
but you're also planning to start selling small-arms?

20:13.110 --> 20:14.790
It isn't a bad deal.

20:15.950 --> 20:18.340
There's only so much one organization can do.

20:18.340 --> 20:21.310
As long as we can secure a stable route, we'll be on easy street.

20:22.040 --> 20:23.720
When will your deal with their boss take place?

20:24.370 --> 20:26.050
I have yet to discuss the details with him.

20:26.050 --> 20:28.750
He's an exceedingly cautious man.

20:28.750 --> 20:31.140
I don't even have a number that I can contact him with.

20:31.500 --> 20:34.350
And you think it's all right to trust a guy like that?

20:43.200 --> 20:45.090
This is a present from Kotetsu.

20:45.940 --> 20:51.520
Most of the weapons that Asaya's members use are what they gave to us.

20:51.520 --> 20:53.040
This sounds too good to be true.

20:54.120 --> 20:56.730
What organization hands out free weapons to their potential business partners?

20:56.730 --> 20:58.210
Doesn't it strike you that this could be a trap?

21:00.200 --> 21:01.950
But they aren't for free.

21:01.950 --> 21:04.150
We're splitting up our original drug with them.

21:04.900 --> 21:06.410
You mean F.A.

21:07.100 --> 21:13.040
This deal also includes the possibilities of Asaya moving its production line to China in the future.

21:13.040 --> 21:15.980
F.A., drug-trafficking, and weapon sales...

21:17.220 --> 21:19.290
May Asaya grow to great heights.

21:27.100 --> 21:29.190
Sounds like some large movements will be made.

21:29.190 --> 21:32.080
Continue to find out more on their agenda so we can make preparations.

21:32.510 --> 21:34.350
What about your end?

21:34.350 --> 21:35.040
Kotetsu, eh?

21:35.880 --> 21:37.960
It's like trying to grab clouds.

21:38.600 --> 21:41.990
The deeper we dig, the harder it becomes for us to catch anything of real substance.

21:41.990 --> 21:45.750
Even if they were petty drug couriers, their influence would have been known to anyone...

21:45.750 --> 21:48.320
But we haven't even found a trace of any of their lower street-level dealers.

21:49.040 --> 21:52.480
Then who is Kuzuya forming his partnership with?

21:52.480 --> 21:56.770
I don't think an imaginary organization would give away a huge load of guns as an early Christmas present.

21:57.300 --> 21:58.760
True.

21:58.760 --> 22:00.420
I'll have the investigation continue without delay,

22:00.420 --> 22:02.890
and if we find anything, I'll let you know right away.

22:02.890 --> 22:03.760
Thanks.

22:04.910 --> 22:05.670
Hal-kun.

22:06.620 --> 22:08.980
Don't do anything reckless.

22:08.980 --> 22:10.160
Never mind me.

22:10.670 --> 22:13.260
How is that guy doing?

22:13.260 --> 22:16.080
Oh, that reminds me. I haven't told you yet.

22:29.360 --> 22:32.330
Kitagishi

23:10.070 --> 23:11.190
All right.

23:28.780 --> 23:29.500
This is...

23:31.690 --> 23:32.700
A trick box?

23:44.940 --> 23:46.070
Ren-kun!

23:50.370 --> 23:51.410
Were you looking for me?

23:52.900 --> 23:54.470
There you are.

23:54.470 --> 23:55.760
How is everything? Think you'll be finished soon?

23:56.600 --> 23:58.160
I'll be done after I put this back.

24:00.790 --> 24:01.790
What's wrong?

24:01.790 --> 24:02.870
You're sweating a lot.

24:02.870 --> 24:04.190
H-Huh?

24:04.190 --> 24:06.650
I guess I must have overexerted myself.

24:07.010 --> 24:10.030
It's nice to see you being so enthusiastic, but don't get yourself sick.

24:10.030 --> 24:11.860
The weather has been getting a lot colder lately.

24:12.340 --> 24:14.340
We might be getting our first snow of the year soon.

24:14.340 --> 24:15.210
Okay.

24:15.210 --> 24:16.270
Thank you for your concern.

24:16.270 --> 24:17.290
I'll take better care of myself.

24:17.790 --> 24:19.870
Well, I'll be going now.

24:19.870 --> 24:21.160
Have a good night!

24:42.490 --> 24:44.040
Too bad for you, Kuzuya...

24:44.040 --> 24:46.980
But Kotetsu's leader says he wants to deal with me directly.

25:24.530 --> 25:25.660
Keep your voice down.

25:28.480 --> 25:28.960
Hal!

25:28.960 --> 25:29.880
Don't move.

25:32.090 --> 25:33.370
I'm so glad you're all right.

25:33.370 --> 25:34.610
Did you find anything?

25:35.350 --> 25:36.730
Sorry, not yet...

25:36.730 --> 25:39.550
But there is a place that caught my interest, so I'll be investigating it next.

25:39.550 --> 25:44.980
I'll pull you off this case myself if you so much as blink the wrong way.

25:44.980 --> 25:46.190
I'll do my best.

25:46.190 --> 25:47.970
Let me know if you need my help on something.

25:47.970 --> 25:48.750
I'll do anything.

25:49.840 --> 25:50.670
Anything?

25:51.870 --> 25:53.400
I want to be useful to you.

25:54.020 --> 25:56.010
Then what if I told you to die?

25:56.390 --> 25:57.700
Would you do that?

25:58.350 --> 26:00.100
T-That's...

26:00.850 --> 26:01.720
But...

26:02.100 --> 26:03.130
But Hal...!

26:05.920 --> 26:06.680
Hal...

26:13.730 --> 26:15.840
Shouhei Kuzuya

26:17.470 --> 26:20.620
Where the hell did Kitagishi disappear to at this important time?

26:21.020 --> 26:22.520
Hey, do you know where Reiji is?

26:22.520 --> 26:23.790
I haven't seen him around today.

26:24.520 --> 26:25.910
I see.

26:27.620 --> 26:30.540
Watch out
for the Matori.

26:31.130 --> 26:32.370
Matori...

26:46.100 --> 26:47.270
All Call Settings Off

26:49.800 --> 26:51.940
Is your investigation showing any progress,

26:53.510 --> 26:55.640
Mr. Matori?

26:56.440 --> 26:57.380
Who is this?

27:05.230 --> 27:06.500
What do you want with me?

27:07.390 --> 27:08.690
Switch.

27:10.520 --> 27:11.370
What?

27:11.370 --> 27:13.960
Is the key to Switch doing well?

27:14.490 --> 27:14.970
You–

27:42.800 --> 27:43.890
Kai.

28:12.400 --> 28:13.780
It's snowing.

28:30.020 --> 28:39.730
The pain comes back with every dawn.

28:43.150 --> 28:53.040
Again, another chapter of my dream fades.

28:56.670 --> 29:03.050
My distant memories are even now sealed anyway,

29:03.300 --> 29:09.390
For I see no need to find the key for its lock.

29:09.390 --> 29:15.770
I still have yet to see the hand.

29:16.020 --> 29:22.400
You still have yet to feel this hand.

29:22.570 --> 29:25.660
Now, without any hesitation,

29:25.910 --> 29:28.870
I simply wish to express this feeling

29:29.200 --> 29:34.790
In a way that it will reach you.

29:34.870 --> 29:42.260
Your Hand...
